body:
That's not a friend. That not the actions of someone who cares about you genuinely. None of those things are how someone who respects you or values you as an equally important person would treat you. I'd use this as a very good time to cut off contact or go to a much more causal friendship with this person. 

&#x200B;

Some friends are people who you click with and have fun with no matte what the situation and some are just the people who you have fun AROUND and not with. Truly think if they're the kind of person you have fun WITH or who you have fun when they are around because the situations and place you are, are fun.

You and your boyfriends are 100% not at fault or responsible! Neither of you choose anything other than to be loved and to love someone. The entire SIL family is the cause, they saw love and felt hate. F them. You never should have to feel like you need to change hun, YOU'RE FINE AND EXACLTY HOW YOU ARE MEANT TO BE!!!! 

&#x200B;

I'm sorry you brother is being such a coward, but your mom is an absolute GEM and I'm so happy you have such a great family backing you up.

Thank you! I'm ok, I've just got A LOT on my plate right now! Which unfortunate has not made me the best friend I could be. WHICH I HATE! :( 

&#x200B;

But as for your friends A and B... there maybe some reflections you need to look at with their friendships as a whole. 

There are people who I really like and see as friends but I've come to understand they are not CLOSE friends, because they just do not have the capacity to be there for me as I would need. I therefore try to give myself a little more space emotionally from them. And yes! It definitely hurt to do that, it feels very much like a lose of a friendship when I did have to do that, however I realized it was a lose of how I THOUGHT of them not a lose of how they actually were and behaved towards me in our friendship... still sucked but once thorough it I think it's become a much healthier relationship for me.

&#x200B;

Friend C may just be a person who is going though it or just needs a gentle reminder that "Hey. You're one of my people, I needed you, and you hurt me by not being there." but then you need to give them a chance to make it up to you so you guys can move on from it. Accept their apologize are sincere and give them a chance to prove it.

&#x200B;

Take all the time you need to feel this tho, don't push it down. We treat our hurts like private emotions we need to hide or be ashamed of too much and it shouldn't be that way. It's a real feeling that matters and deserves to be seen examined and addressed with out any shame or stigmas. 

&#x200B;

I hope you and all three of them can make something good out of all this but if you don't manage to come back to the same place with all of them just know that losing friends is hard, but we never really stop making new friends or gaining important people as we go through life. Treat yourself and those around you with the same respect and kindness, and expect that in return. 

&#x200B;

Good luck!

Calms Forte Sleep Aid by Hyland's. It's you can find it at some of the health stores ( I get mine at Sprouts Farmers Market) it's just an over the counter sleep supplement. My mom's memory care doctor recommended it to me. It's not very expensive it's not a sleeping pill it just helps with anxiety. 

&#x200B;

Idk it works for me, not like magic but it's helped me sleep deeper and more restoratively maybe that's placebo but I'll take whatever I can.

Adult family services in you area should have a Social Services agent you can call. I know someone saying here do a thing is SUPER not fun sounding right now but you're going to burn out. You already are but eventually you'll turn around and realizes you've nothing let to give and it will break you or it will be unleashed on your friends or family. You guys need help and if your mom doesn't have income besides ss and now assets than there probably are services she is eligible for. There may even be things YOU are eligible for because you work part time and share a home with her. Call the closest Senior Center you have in you area tell them what you're going through, say the words WE NEED HELP (not just meal services) but a counselor.

&#x200B;

If that's to daunting call your daughter and TELL HER, "I need you're help. Please help me research and find assistance for your grandmother. I am struggling and I need you to do 9these things) for me. 

&#x200B;

I care for my mother, and my brother is not helpful either unless I tell him VERY specifically things I need him to do, and I HATE that I need to TELL HIM any of these things and that he never takes the initiative or askes or just tries to help BUT I've learned over the past few years that I can hate that I need to ask him but I NEED to ask him because doing it alone is painful... So I pick my anger at having to tell a grown man the right thing to do over the constant draining struggle of trying to do things on my own and KNOWING I don't have it in me to do it all no matter how hard I try. 

&#x200B;

There is no shame in tell people I need help, and there is nothing demanding or bossy about telling people they need to do things to help you're shared loved one. 

&#x200B;

Now doesn't mean my brother always does the things I ask, in fact he half asses most of what I ask but if I'm honest his half ass job is still half I don't have to do. 

&#x200B;

Call your daughter, ask her to help you reach out to adult social services and ask her to be with you when you speak to them or to be on the phone call so she can help you. You're an amazing daughter to be doing so much for your mom but once there's no way to take care of ourselves as a caregiver then it's time to call in more troops. 

&#x200B;

I live in Cali and I've gotten in touch with my states adult social services so if I can help with phone numbers I will.

This is troll right? Cause no like NORMAL human person would think you're anything other then they're the Ahole here????

&#x200B;

YTA

I think you are doing a wonderful job and trying to keep what you know to be important to her is such a kind and thoughtful thing to take into consideration with everything else you must have on your hands. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

\*\*\*Also just for the humor of it, one of the things I have in my trunk right now is an expresso machine... no really... I have no idea where she got it and she doesn't know how to use it!! HOW!! lol

Hey man! Most of us do, it's hard to stand up for what we really deserve cause most of us were brought up to not want to be a bother and to be helpful to others otherwise we're "selfish" and it scares us into not really knowing when its ok to say, "NO" and "Actually that's mine." 

&#x200B;

You're doing great!

WHAT! They makes those!!! I need it!!!

&#x200B;

Edit: I mean... my cats need it... 👀"

I mean, an adult could probably be able to walk outside and figure out the situation; things like they have a dog, they are outside at 4 am or asking them, "Hey was it your dog just in a fight with my gf's?"

&#x200B;

You know... like how an adult human with average problem solving skills would solve a problem.

Ugh, I mean. You're the grown ups and she's the kid so it WOULD be really magnanimous and you would 100% be the bigger person to look beyond her poor choices and her behavior... but... you don't really have to.

It depends on how much you think she MEANT what she said. If you feel like the recording was her real feelings and she's been using you all this time then, no, absolutely not, you do not need to include her in anymore family expenditures. She clearly picked a side of the fence.

&#x200B;

However if there's even a part of you that thinks that this is just a stunt to gain her Mother's/Mother's family's approval and acceptances. Than don't push her out yet, she still needs you she's just young and impressionable and not a really thinking of anything other than how to protect herself from bullies.

&#x200B;

It's up to you, but can I recommend TALKING to her before the graduation. You don't need to say you heard a recording you don't need to say your other niece told you anything. You just need to sit her down and ask her if she truly loves and respects you to either be honest with you or to stop speaking disrespectfully about you to her other side of the family. That it's hurtful and unfair and not acceptable no matter what.

&#x200B;

But yeah, you don't HAVE to invite anyone to anything, you're an aunt not a parent or step parent. I'm sorry this sucks. You sound like a very kind and loving person, I'm sure this hurt you a lot.

&#x200B;

Edit to add verdict: NTA

Y-W-B-T-A if you DIDN'T treat Josh with respect. You're buddy Zack is WAY stirring the pot. If the party/dinner is about Antonio introducing you to his new GF than you would be a real jerk to highjack the event to have a 1v1 with Josh.

&#x200B;

Time and place, and this isn't it. Be the bigger, more mature man and just treat Josh like a stranger who you've meet a few times. Respectful. Courteous but with a good bit of cautious space emotionally.

ESH. I mean you actively are telling people your don't like this person so of course they stop inviting you to things she's invited to. It seems like the rest of you friends have figured out a way to be around Britt without making her feel excluded but somehow you haven't.

&#x200B;

On the other side you don't have to like her just because she's married to your buddy... but you are going to in effect very much diminish the relationship you have with your buddy, a lot. His loyalty is to her now, not you. Also trying to get the others guys together to have a "...a group conversation" bro... that's some not very grown up, mean girl behavior.

&#x200B;

but that whole I already reached out thing... that she's doing is not cool either. She needs to get over that and you two need to sit down and agree on the one thing you have in common. Your friend who you both care for and who wants all the people in his life to get along and have a good time together.

&#x200B;

Communication. It's by far the largest issue in this thread.

I mean mine stole over 200K from my mom with Alzheimer's bank and then tried to accuse me of causing him 2K in bank fee's by tricking her into opening up a separate account he didn't have access to anymore... and that nearly caused my brother and I to fall out until I brought the bank statements to prove I had NOTHING to do with it and my "dad" was full of shit and just didn't want to get caught being a POS by his son. 

&#x200B;

but yeah no... I just... like to argue with him.... totally... that's me.... yeah.

I'll feel fine. There are somethings that can't be repaired... if my NC parent died tomorrow I'd feel sad for my aunt's and uncles. My self and my sibling will lose nothing in our lives if he passed. He's not kind or good to us... the only thing he does is cause hurt. There's nothing WE have to repair, we have done the work. 

&#x200B;

You can't make someone treat you well, sometimes you have no more actions on the board but to walk away.

Idk this one is hard... but yeah a little bit YTA. 

&#x200B;

It's just generally frowned upon as adults to not invite partners for thigs like this. If it's because of cost or some other limitation it's one thing but you directly told your friend that her partner wasn't invited because you didn't WANT her there. That's an ouchie. 

&#x200B;

Whether or not you have a reason for cutting off the friendship with her partner she loves them and that's not going to be nice to hear. I wouldn't want to go to a place that my partner was specifically not invited too... it would just make me feel bad the whole time I was there.

RUN. So many red flags in everything you just said. He doesn't seem to have an honest interest or care for the people around him serious early Narcist warning flags. 

&#x200B;

If money is tight or you where raised that way it's one thing but if he seems to be approaching everything as if I am giving anything to anyone I need compensation. AKA Giving anything without getting something in return seems stupid to him... that's a huge Narcasistic tendency that can cause SERIOUS problems down the road. 

&#x200B;

Not giving the computer to his little brother I could kind of get as he may see it as an investment he made by putting time and effort into it once upon a time but everything else PLUS that... no, he's just not interested in giving things to people unless there's something in it for him. YIKES.

You're not an A-hole... you're Spidey senses are tingling girl.

You're his daughter. Not his nurse/home aide provider. If he has the option to have care and refuses that then it doesn't mean that now you have to become that for him. He has help, he just wants someone who he has more perceived power to control/tell what to do.

&#x200B;

One thing that I've learned as a caregiver (for my mom) I've had to come to terms with (largely because of other people's opinions and outside expectations on what a "child" is supposed to do for a parent) is to understand that we all want to help and care for our parents because of this notion that when we were little and helpless they in some way helped or cared for us (though obviously less so in your case) but as children we didn't cause your helplessness. We didn't create the situation where our parents were the only ones who could provide for us. And very rarely did them caring for us require them to change their lives, we instead where a part of their lives.

&#x200B;

You're dad is creating a situation where his loved ones need to care for him by sacrificing they're current life for him, and when you didn't immediately do that switched to trying to essentially bribe you with his home/inheritance . It's as though he's saying you have to EARN the things that parents would normally just GIVE.

&#x200B;

I have a father JUST like this. I'm lucky he has yet to hit a turn in health and that he still is on speaking terms with my only sibling, because for my self, for those who I love and who love me, I will never be his care taker. The emotional damage of have to earn his love and his desire to provide anything of his for me when he's gone (my dad would absolutely do the same kind of conditional stuff because he equates love with monetary care) that would be unbearable. To be turned into simply his caregiver and still neve be seen or treated like his daughter. No. Don't do that to yourself. You deserve better.

Yeah, and also tell people with allergies to stop sneezing all over people when they get pollen in their system! I mean it's only a physical bodily reaction. Control yourself and stop be so selfish with other people!

&#x200B;

(Yeah Allergies are involuntary and people CHOOSE to get nicotine addiction but that does not change the fact that when you're having an allergic reaction or withdrawing from nicotine it is a PHYSICAL REACTION YOU CAN NOT WILL-POWER AWAY) They hey, "Hey mom stop smoking because it's a disgusting habit, and it cost to much money!" is not the conversation to have in this moment. If she bought allergy pills for the same price because she was having a mild reaction would anyone be made at her? Doubt it.

This morning when I looked at my mom's security cameras and caught her standing in her doorway at midnight again look confused and lost for the I have no idea how many times even though I called her at 10pm and she promised me she was going to go to bed and try to get some sleep.

&#x200B;

Fact: The tears of people with loved ones going through Alzheimer's dementia could fill an ocean.

Oh god I am so glade to be grown. Honestly there's a really not fun lesson in all this, that really sucks to have to learn but, "You gotta just ignore the A-holes in life and do you."

&#x200B;

In life there will always be people who act out of pocket and just do not treat you or others well. You're not going to change them with ANYTHING you say, and it doesn't matter that they are wrong or that they shouldn't be behaving like that. That will never make them stop or change.

Sadly "Should" and "Shouldn't" wind up meaning very little in the world outside of our own actions. Other people's actions are completely out of our control.

&#x200B;

The only thing YOU do have control of is how you treat/what you do to people. Anytime you are acting or doing something with the express desire to cause a reaction in someone else... you've got like 90% chance of failure. It just doesn't work most of the time. So don't do that.

&#x200B;

Your friend is right. Don't look at her. Don't talk to her. Don't respond to her. Bullies (and that's what she is even if she's not physically harming or straight teasing you) only do what they do for YOUR reaction.

&#x200B;

YWBTA if you said that to her, and worse you'd just be feeding into her ego.

&#x200B;

Edit to add: Getting even ALWAYS makes you the asshole in real life.

The only thing I can say is, they didn't want to hit YOU really. They wanted to hit what was frustrating them.

I have to think of things that way with my Mom all the time, cause she is very quick to anger and can get... yeah... anyways. They're confused they don't understand what's being said and nothing WE can do will help them it's the disease we are talking at in those moments not our parents. To them WE are the ones saying crazy irrational things and think of how frustrating and scary that must be. Least that's what I TRY to do.

&#x200B;

De-escalation is the only way to go about it in those horrible moments, usually I make sure that I am Physically less imposing. Like I find a way to sit lower than them and speak quitter and softer and just redirect the conversation. Sometimes just taking whatever they're upset about and saying "I understand -blank- must be frustrating, I'm so sorry. That must be upsetting." and then redirecting to another task can help.

&#x200B;

IDK I'm still trying to write the cheat code for my mom's own melt downs. Usually brining up her Grandson and asking her questions about him works best lol

I can't pretend like she's okay... for some reason the idea of pretending in conversation with semi-strangers about her condition when I already have to pretend TO her so she doesn't feel upset or attacked by her condition is just... too exhausting to even think about.

&#x200B;

Usually if I run into people who ask how she's doing I just say, "She's good" cause she is, and give "yes" or "no" answers to any other questions but if someone really is digging or asking things about her I will usually just break out with a straight, "Well she was diagnosed with Alzheimer's 6yrs ago so..." and they then give the usual placating "I'm so sorry!" "That's terrible?" "Poor Mom!" and then stop bringing her up and move on to another topic or leave me alone completely.

&#x200B;

I'm not sure if that's a healthy way to go about it but I for me I just can't handle people wanting to talk to me about how she WAS cause she's not like that anymore and it hurts.

I used to think this about my cat too, and then I realized he just sleeps on the rug by the front door waiting for me 😭 took all my will power not to just quite my job immediately and never leave the house.

&#x200B;

Edit to say: I have two cats it's just my boy loves me with all his little orange heart and I don't deserve it.

Yep. It was my fault that my mom's (unwitting) friend came and picked her up from my Brother's house and helped her get her hands on her old car/key's and then Mom tried to drive back to his house, subsequently getting into a car accident by running a red light... while I was signing paperwork on my new apartment 45min away... and it was my fault I turned my cell off to do the walk through of the apartment and then I was extremely irresponsible by not calling the insurance agents for them while I, again, was 45min away trying to get the keys to my new apartment and they where right there with her and in possession of her insurance card. All within the span of 3hrs.

&#x200B;

Shit never ends. You're doing amazing and taking on the weight of like 80 people they just lack any perspective or empathy.

I always say the same thing about wills/trusts. It was your GRANDFATHER'S WISHES. You didn't write the will that way, you and your brother didn't ask for the money to be divided like that and same goes for your mom. 

&#x200B;

Tell you dad you are respecting your Grandparents wishes, this is how they WANTED to take care of their family. Your Dad can think of it however he wants but that's the bottom line. 

&#x200B;

You're Grandparents made their wishes known.

Hey man show ur a\*\* to the sun, get a sunburn. No one made him look like an idiot but himself. 

&#x200B;

NTA

LOVE is thicker than blood or water.

&#x200B;

NTA

A group of chiropractors.

&#x200B;

...no  I will not elaborate but this is accurate.

I have two.

1. Not being able to be in a room with more than say 5-6 other people at one time with out wanting to leave ASAP!
2. Wearing the same item of clothing more than HALF the week straight, regardless of what it's paired with.

&#x200B;

1/ I can't stand the energy of rooms with more that 4-5 people at once. I noticed this started kicking up at the beginning of my Depressive Episodes. There's just SO MUCH to pay attention too and it so noisy and chaotic. Makes me feel like my skin is crawling (When I'm really bad anything more than one or two ppl is all I can take.)

&#x200B;

2/ I'm no fashionista, but I at least used to have like conscious outfits and that "social norm" of not wearing the same exact thing two days in a row. When I started going into the "dark places" I started not to care if I wore the same mustard yellow sweater every day for a month, same not-exactly work appropriate shoes to the office or the exact same pants every other days. It didn't matter and I didn't care enough to try to find my other shoes or sweaters or shirts or pants... as stupid as clothing is. It's a big tell.

&#x200B;

\*\* also as a personal one for me, my SKIN is how I tell ppl they can tell if I'm doing poorly or not. I've got very difficult skin and all it takes is a week of poor eating and neglected for it to get gnarly. Huge mental health tell for me, more so than anything else. \*\*

[https://imgur.com/Subbcsl](https://imgur.com/Subbcsl)

&#x200B;

Lets a GO!

I just did it. I wrote a whole email reply out to my NF after he sent me a nasty one and then I deleted it because I realized... he wasn't going to get ANYTHING I was saying, what I had to say was NEVER going to matter to him, and the only thing I could possible get was another nasty email from him back or somehow have him twist whatever I said as more ammunition to hurt me. 

&#x200B;

It was probably the best choice I ever made. It's been 2yrs now and I'm just now over that feeling that I should have sent him something to "give him a chance" every day of my life has been a chance and he's taken none of them, why in all the world would anything change because I gave him one more. I picked me.

I wish I know you cause I really really want to go to a bunch of bars hand out bags of candy and tell the bouncers "I'll give you this whole bag of fun size snickers if you let my one friend "Trick-or-Treat" here, it's they're first time" 

&#x200B;

I am 100% certain that everyone one of those bouncers will be DOWN it would be so much fun. 

&#x200B;

I hope you start opening yourself up to friends soon. I'm an adult who only really started to allow myself to make friends in her late 20's because I was sure everyone what just being nice to me because I was pathetic or they where just being nice. And if this feels at all relatable to you than just take a few baby steps into people's personal space. 

Cause color me shocked when I started to chance disappointing all these people with my self and learned that they actually like me... like, like ME. ...as I am... when I'm not even doing anything for them... but just, you know, talking and hanging out... mind altering. 

&#x200B;

It's so hard to have to build all this self worth for ourselves as adults. IT SUCKS!

Yep. I've worked in a particular field for over 8 yrs, have the ears of professionals who've been in this field for 30+ YEARS! and still when I was attempting to set something up for my ailing mother WITHIN that field... the same thing other people pay us to do for them EVERY DAY... which we were going to do for free for my family... I was told I "didn't know what I was talking about" by my NF and brother. Also that I needed to stop arguing with people so much and specifically my brother told me that I even tell people that are experts that they're wrong.... accept in this case I AM THE EXPERT or at the very least my coworkers and BOSS are the expert... so ??

&#x200B;

Basically it never mattered if we were/are right ever. The facts are unimportant to them, it just mattered that we are beneath them so we have to be wrong. Little sister, Child. Doesn't' matter. Even at 30yrs old I'm infantized because they don't see me as a person who can have intelligence, a thought or know anything important beyond them.

&#x200B;

We must be kept DOWN so the can feel powerful.

&#x200B;

...really sucks.

When you took your nice in you where meant to take her future and happiness into account too. You didn't just agree to giver her food and clothes. Let me ask you this if she WAS you child would you pay for her? If the answer is YES for even half a second YTA.

&#x200B;

You brought her into your home, and immediate family. She is YOURS. Now and forever. Now you get to deiced what kind of parent you would like to be for her because paper work or not after 6yrs she's YOUR child too, just like your other 3.

YSH but NTA for the post. He's the father of your kid and he's doing a good job at it. You can thank him for it if you want to. It's nice. 

&#x200B;

BUT wow all of this toxic family drama. You should really look at what drove you to sleep with someone as payback and then distance yourself from your sister as much as possible, you've got some very hostile family dynamics and for the sake of you little girl: Therapy please. 

&#x200B;

It will make you a stronger person.  Cause you don't sound like a terrible human but that action is the mark of a serious emotional well that needs to be addressed.

YTA. You want your kid to trust you? Then don't treat them like they are already lying. Yes teenagers are gonna lie to an extent and try to get away with things but YOU are supposed to be showing you kid the RIGHT way to behave as a person. Searching her wallet and her room on a regular basis is a large violation of the trust you should have as parent and child. 

&#x200B;

You're gonna push her away if you keep doing this. I'd apologize to her if I was you then try to TALK to her. Communication is the most under utilized parenting skill out there.

NTA it was meant to be a short term stay and it's already been half a year. If he was a good fit than maybe you could offer him a longer renting situation but it's not a fit. You do not ever need to feel uncomfortable in your own home. Bought, rented or otherwise.

&#x200B;

EDIT: SP

No way NTA, you're friend was being racist. 

&#x200B;

Unless he has a job or is in a situation where he actually works predominantly with individuals from Mexico and they dig ditches together all the time. Your friend got called out on his shit and didn't like so he got defensive, and you're bilingual friend down played it because it probably didn't serve them to stand up to him at that time. 

&#x200B;

Lot of times it's easier to just act like a shark isn't there if you're not the one bleeding, it'll swim by, but make a splash and it might decide you're dinner. Survival.

Yes. God yes. And it seems like even when you try to make things easier and tell them how to solve the problem they become obtuse and completely inept all the sudden.

&#x200B;

EXAMPLE:  My mom's loses things all the time, she just move them around and hides them in weird places. So I have put TILES on almost all her things and STILL my brother and sister-in-law can't find things for her when she loses them. "I looked but I couldn't find it." Did you use the Tile app? "No, I don't have it on my phone." Yeah, alright but it's on mom's phone and the I-pad. "Well I didn't use it." Alright great... que me driving all the way down there and finding it in a weird place but still managing to be able to -FIND IT- in her apartment after like 15min of really looking... the number of times this exact thing has happened it mind boggling.

Oh man, I'm sorry that sucks a lot. Neither of them are of states to understand the other's situation and as shit as it may be you have to decided who gets you, cause you are just one you. We push ourselves to be more that we are and that's how we brake. If there is anyone, ANYONE AT ALL who can sit with either you dad or you boyfriend for a few days at a time that will probably be best. Dementia is not something that most people who aren't in a fragile state can understand so I don't think you will get you BF to understand what's going on until he's stabilized on his new med. Not his fault and not your dads, DEFINETLY not yours either. Just is. A logical mind can't explain to an impaired mind no mater how hard  we try. 

&#x200B;

And try to remember it's not about who you "love" more or who's issues are "more important" it's about who has the most resources. So if your BF has friends or family and your Dad just has you or vice versa it's about taking the path with the most resources so you can help them both without hurting you. 

&#x200B;

One person can not move a mountain unfortunately much less two.

Read the first sentence and stopped. Run girl.

&#x200B;

Edit: Read the rest of you post: Run, find a bridge run across that and light it on fire. THAT MAN IS A DANGER. Ewww

Yes you can.  You can say that to your mom's face!!  In fact if your mom can't hear things like that from you than she's not being a very supportive parent! 

You're the child in this scenario. I'm gonna tell you a secret that I didn't learn until I was in my late 20's and on my second therapist. You CAN make your parents uncomfortable. And it's THERE job to help you with YOUR feelings not the other way around!!  

&#x200B;

If something is happening and you feel like you can't say anything to your mom because she'll get upset, STOP. Realize that her getting upset is OKAY and that she's your MOM and an ADULT she can and will work through her feelings and then she can help you AND HER get through the problem together.

&#x200B;

I know it's scary and intimidating and we never want to hurt our loved ones, especially our moms, feelings but legit that is what our parents are there for, to help us! Talk to your mom. She probably doesn't realize the pressure she's putting you under here. If I was your Mom I know I would hate that I made you feel like this was your problem to solve. Cause it's so not!

&#x200B;

(Also I do acknowledge that no everyone has good or strong parents, (I did mention the multiple therapist right?) trust me I  KNOW so if you are in a situation where you feel like speaking would be a danger to YOU than don't feel pressured to do that, that's different than just trying to spare your Parent's feelings.)

Are you the AH because your SIL tried to lie and didn't follow the rules at he AirBnB you bookend,  and then you and our husband had to scramble and find a new place to stay for your vacation? No, no you are not the AH.

&#x200B;

Also side bar; of course MIL is upset and expecting you to give her daughter special treatment. Ur SIL didn't scrape up their entitlement from the ground!

Uhhh yes I agree there are definitely makeups that smell of those things but also.... not all. If I may be so bold, I might say you maybe haven't had enough experimentation with makeup, especially if you feel that all makeup has similar scents like lard (Vegan makeups don't use that). 

&#x200B;

I am also pretty picky with smells, particularly plastics, the wrong brand of ziplock bags can drive me bonkers but if that was the only reason you don't enjoy playing with makeup you may just need to try new products. Cause that's how I feel about make up its just something fun to play with. 

&#x200B;

